#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hubctl: run Chef's Prodigy hubs on a single-node k3s cluster behind Cloudflare.

Standard library only; drives `kubectl`. See docs/SPEC-hosted-platform.md
section 5.6 and deploy/README.md. Settings live in ``<root>/.env`` (``--root``,
``HUBCTL_ROOT`` or /srv/chefslegacy); everything else lives in the cluster:

    chefs-system   Traefik middlewares, the backup CronJob and its RBAC, the R2
                   credentials Secret, the llm-gateway (Deployment, Service, PVC,
                   Secret with the vendor keys); later: platform, provisioner
    chefs-hubs     one Secret + StatefulSet + Service + Ingress + PVC per hub,
                   default-deny NetworkPolicies
    kube-system    Traefik's HelmChartConfig and the Origin CA default TLSStore

Commands: init, create, remove [--purge], list, status, rotate-key, login-link,
gateway-token <name>, usage [name] [--from --to], backup <name|all>,
restore <name> <archive>, upgrade [name|all],
render [name|all] [--json] (what would be applied) and render --reference DIR (the
checked-in deploy/k8s/*.yaml set, regenerated whenever the manifests change).
Tests: python3 -I -m unittest discover -s deploy/tests
"""

